# SPDX-License-Identifier: Apache-2.0
# Lumen OS PUBLIC images, both editions; only Lumen OS without Google (ro.z9x.gms=0) uses it (image path
# /system/etc/init/z9x_gapps.rc; script /system/etc/z9x/z9x_gapps.sh 0755, allow-list
# /system/etc/z9x/gapps_allow.txt 0644, sysconfig layer /system/etc/z9x/gapps/sysconfig/z9x-gapps.xml 0644).
# See z9x_gapps.sh: the user's own Google services add-on in z9x_gapps<slot>, checked and overlaid.
# exec at post-fs-data, like z9x_blobs.rc (default mount namespace): before zygote-start, so PackageManager
# and SystemConfig see the add-on at their first scan. Without the partition: three getprops and a test
# (sys.z9x.gapps=none). With it: one read-only ext4 mount, ~25 metadata-only finds, six overlay mounts:
# about 60 short processes, roughly 0.2 s. One 2 s budget for the whole run (bad:slow when used up), so at
# most about 3 s with the mount's own timeout (the PWM watchdog margin is ~7 s).
on post-fs-data
    exec u:r:su:s0 root root -- /system/bin/sh /system/etc/z9x/z9x_gapps.sh
